created: 2026-09-06
expires: 2026-09-20
# CI-6 (11-continuous-improvement-criterion.md § 6): enforce-reviewer-readonly.sh's
# cache deny began refusing writes it previously allowed (round 4's fix, T-013 /
# INV-5), so it ships with a shadow period per CI-6's default rather than a clean
# flip -- the user was not available to record a clean-flip decision, and CI-6
# applies its default when no such decision is recorded.
#
# During this shadow period, ONLY for the verdict-cache deny in
# enforce-reviewer-readonly.sh: a decision the PREVIOUS control (the one in
# effect before round 4's fix) would ALSO have allowed logs one line to
# .squad/log/gate-shadow.md and exits 0 instead of refusing. Constraint 1 of
# CI-6: this never affects a decision the previous control already refused --
# not a literal-spelling match (already denied before round 4) and never a
# Block from a failed verdict check. Missing file, or a missing, malformed, or
# lapsed expires:, means NOT shadowing -- enforcing, per CI-6's own text.
#
# This repository (Abies) receives enforce-reviewer-readonly.sh's verdict-cache
# deny for the first time as part of the squad-flow v2.1 delta, so it opens its
# own 14-day shadow period here rather than inheriting the template's -- the
# template's own shadow governs only the template repository's copy of the
# hook. expires: is 14 days from created:, the CI-6 maximum for an initial
# shadow. See the template's `.claude/docs/flow-changelog.md` for the fuller
# history of this control (round 4 introduction, round 5/6 fixes below).
#
# 09-review-verdict.md round 5, finding 4: this file previously claimed "the
# shadow logic ... is not yet implemented" and "this changeset was built under
# a no-shadow decision" and "this file is inert" -- none of that was true; no
# such decision is recorded anywhere else in this repository, and it shipped a
# 30-day expires: against CI-6's 14-day maximum. Both are fixed here: the
# log-and-allow path is implemented in enforce-reviewer-readonly.sh, and
# expires: is 14 days from created:, the CI-6 maximum for an initial shadow.
#
# The user -- and only the user -- may extend this once, by at most 14 more
# days, as an appended entry below this line (per CI-6 constraint 3). An agent
# extending its own expiry has built the laundering shape CI-6 exists to
# prevent.
#
# 09-review-verdict.md round 6, finding B: the extension above is now
# actually read. enforce-reviewer-readonly.sh takes the LAST expires: line
# in this file (the appended extension, if one exists), not the first --
# a prior revision `break`d at the first match and silently ignored any
# extension appended per the paragraph above. It also now reads created:
# and refuses to shadow (enforces instead) when the LAST expires: is more
# than 28 days after created:, or more than 14 days after the FIRST
# expires: -- CI-6 constraint 3's absolute ceiling, checked rather than
# merely documented.
#
# SQUAD_NOW: enforce-reviewer-readonly.sh and its tests support an ISO
# YYYY-MM-DD override of the wall clock used to evaluate this file,
# TEST-ONLY and honoured only when SQUAD_TEST_HARNESS=1 is ALSO set (only
# tests/blindness.sh exports that combination). Setting SQUAD_NOW to a
# date before the expires: above -- under that same test harness --
# revives an otherwise-lapsed shadow; nothing in a normal agent or
# maintainer shell can do this, since SQUAD_TEST_HARNESS is never set
# outside the test suite.
